flowchart TB
    accTitle: What a tap on a player does
    accDescr: Ada plays, and a tap on Bob switches. The extension renews Bob's session at Autodarts with his parked token or, when Autodarts refuses the token, with his remembered password. When that fails, the page stays as it is and no token is lost: Bob has to sign in again when Autodarts refused him, and a tap later tries again when Autodarts couldn't be reached. Otherwise the extension saves Bob's fresh token, parks Ada's session from the page, still valid at Autodarts, writes Bob's session into the page and reloads it, and every other Autodarts tab reloads as Bob.

    tap["Ada plays,<br>a tap on Bob"]
    renew["Renew Bob's session<br>at Autodarts: with his<br>parked token, or with<br>his remembered password<br>when the token is refused"]
    stays["The page stays as it is,<br>no token is lost<br>refused: Bob signs in again<br>no answer: tap again later"]
    save["Save Bob's fresh token"]
    park["Park Ada's session<br>from the page; it stays<br>valid at Autodarts"]
    write["Write Bob's session<br>into the page, reload it"]
    others["Every other Autodarts tab<br>reloads as Bob"]

    tap --> renew
    renew -- "renewed" --> save
    save --> park --> write --> others
    renew -. "not renewed" .-> stays
    others ~~~ stays

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef failed fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class tap person
    class renew,save,park,write bot
    class others done
    class stays failed
